WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.263 --> 00:00:01.558
(fast orchestral music)

00:00:01.558 --> 00:00:02.997
- [Voiceover] The penny
farthing was the first machine

00:00:02.997 --> 00:00:04.914
to be called a bicycle.

00:00:09.212 --> 00:00:10.750
(bell ringing)

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:14.917
They're old, they're funny,
and for some, still a big deal.

00:00:16.125 --> 00:00:17.739
- Sometimes I go into a local bike shop

00:00:17.739 --> 00:00:18.877
just for a bit of a joke and ask

00:00:18.877 --> 00:00:20.033
if they've got a tire to fit my bike,

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:24.806
and then bring them outside
to have a look at it.

00:00:24.806 --> 00:00:27.814
(upbeat music)

00:00:27.814 --> 00:00:29.978
People find the penny
farthing almost hypnotic.

00:00:29.978 --> 00:00:31.774
I don't know why, I can't explain it,

00:00:31.774 --> 00:00:33.201
but people just love seeing it.

00:00:33.201 --> 00:00:35.835
And it's just a real pleasure
to share it with people.

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:38.149
- [Voiceover] Richard, being
an already avid bike racer,

00:00:38.149 --> 00:00:39.829
discovered penny farthing racing

00:00:39.829 --> 00:00:42.198
on an Internet forum one night.

00:00:42.198 --> 00:00:44.115
- So I entered immediately, very excited.

00:00:44.115 --> 00:00:46.158
And then realized that a, I
don't have a penny farthing

00:00:46.158 --> 00:00:48.045
and b, I don't know how
to ride a penny farthing.

00:00:48.045 --> 00:00:50.747
- [Voiceover] But he
overcame those hurdles.

00:00:50.747 --> 00:00:52.485
- [Richard] I'm a current UK champion,

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:54.682
so I've got a title to defend.

00:00:54.682 --> 00:00:55.806
- [Voiceover] But penny farthing racing

00:00:55.806 --> 00:00:59.973
isn't as easy as it looks,
and it sure doesn't look easy.

00:00:59.973 --> 00:01:01.409
- [Richard] It's a very
dangerous machine to ride.

00:01:01.409 --> 00:01:04.673
You're sat up on top, on the
point of balance virtually.

00:01:04.673 --> 00:01:05.978
So, if anything goes wrong you tend

00:01:05.978 --> 00:01:08.330
to be going head first
over the front of the bike.

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:11.042
- [Voiceover] The bikes can
be up to five feet tall,

00:01:11.042 --> 00:01:13.600
and that height has its benefits.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:15.604
- [Richard] Racing one of
these bikes, pretty high up

00:01:15.604 --> 00:01:17.269
you get a fantastic view of the crowd.

00:01:17.269 --> 00:01:19.137
It's the best way to see the event here

00:01:19.137 --> 00:01:20.296
I always tell people.

00:01:20.296 --> 00:01:21.768
- [Voiceover] Height
is not the only benefit

00:01:21.768 --> 00:01:23.529
the penny farthing has.

00:01:23.529 --> 00:01:25.298
- A big difference between
riding a penny farthing

00:01:25.298 --> 00:01:29.154
and a normal bike is you
can't slow down very quickly.

00:01:29.154 --> 00:01:30.484
You got to watch the road ahead.

00:01:30.484 --> 00:01:31.568
But I find the biggest difference

00:01:31.568 --> 00:01:33.055
is the smiles on people's faces.

00:01:33.055 --> 00:01:33.996
When you ride one of these things,

00:01:33.996 --> 00:01:35.534
people just love to see it.

00:01:35.534 --> 00:01:38.408
They smile, they wave, they
pull up to take photographs.

00:01:38.408 --> 00:01:40.399
I've had so many conversations with people

00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:42.168
I would never, ever
meet without this bike.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:43.156
And that's the joy of it.

00:01:43.156 --> 00:01:47.239
People just love seeing
it and talking about it.

